// (G.chapters.moments: Sunday dinner, the Kettle Corner, the festival moments, Dad's seasonal chair): these are separate evenings.
// Every scene needs its Chapter (`when.chapter`), so the arcs never run ahead of the main story or give anything away.
//
// ARC    { person, title, premise, thread, scenes: Scene[6-9] }   built by _rel_kit arc(): scene ids are '<person>.<key>'.
// SCENE  { id, n, title, when, place, invite (their text), window, steps, fx, prev, ask?: [question, answer] }
//        A scene arrives as an invitation and sits in My Day as an idea with their name until the player goes. It never expires.
//        `ask` is the thread left open: later "Ask about..." offers the question and they give the answer.
//        The last scene of an arc sets '<person>_arc_done' and hands over a page (rel_pages.js).
// =============================================================================
